 "summary": "Mostly no. After price retested a fair value gap, or entered a bearish gap, it did no better than after a random candle on 1h, 4h or daily. The result that holds up is on 1h: while price stayed above a bullish gap's high, it was 0.22% further ahead 20 candles later than after a random candle, and this showed at every horizon tested.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Riding a bullish gap (price above the gap high, 1h)",
   "verdict": "edge",
   "text": "On 1h, price moved further up than after random candles. This holds without its strongest stretch and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles."
  },
  {
   "use": "Riding a bullish gap on daily candles",
   "verdict": "fragile",
   "text": "It sits just above the luck band on daily, but only because of one stretch between Aug 16, 2021 and Sep 6, 2021. Without that stretch it is chance."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying the retest of a bullish gap",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "When price crossed down into a bullish gap's high or middle, it did no better than after random candles on 1h, 4h or daily."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting into a bearish gap",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "When price crossed up into a bearish gap's middle, stayed below a bearish gap's low or broke a bullish gap's low, the moves landed inside the luck band on every timeframe."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, price stayed above a bullish gap's high on 22,577 candles, which form 1,941 separate moves. Twenty candles later, price was 0.22% further ahead than after random candles. The luck band runs from -0.10% to 0.13%. The result holds without its strongest stretch, Jan 6–12, 2021, and at 10, 20, 50 and 100 candles.",
  "The 1h result comes from ETH and SOL, not BTC. SOL was 0.41% ahead of random and ETH 0.21% ahead. BTC was only 0.04% ahead, inside its band. On ETH the gap disappears at 100 candles.",
  "Higher timeframes don't confirm it. On 4h the same condition was 0.35% ahead of random, inside a band that reaches 0.39%. On daily it was 3.77% ahead, just above the band. That daily result rests on 20 entries between Aug 16, 2021 and Sep 6, 2021, and without them it is chance.",
  "Retest entries show nothing. On 1h, price crossing down through a bullish gap's middle gave 1,864 entries and finished 0.14% ahead of random, inside the band. On 4h, SOL's 1.66% after gap-middle retests came from signals on Nov 5–7, 2020.",
  "The bearish side shows nothing either. Price crossing up into a bearish gap's middle, or holding below its low, stayed inside the luck band on 1h, 4h and daily. On 1h, SOL's cross into a bearish gap middle looked 0.50% worse than random. That result comes from two signals on Sep 9, 2020, and only shows at 10 and 20 candles.",
  "On a long bot running 1h ETH or SOL, price above a bullish gap's high can serve as a filter beside your main start condition. The DCA orders and take profit still do most of the work. On BTC, on 4h or daily, gap conditions add nothing measurable. For gap retest entries and bearish gap shorts, the data gives no reason to add them."
 ],
